      "content": "## Active session guidance\nItems are listed oldest to newest within each section. When guidance conflicts, prefer the later item.\n### Goals\n- [09:03:23] User wants to know the recent project history and timeline.\n- [09:03:50] User wants to know the recent project history and timeline of the project.\n- [09:07:04] Understand recent project history and timeline.\n- [09:43:54] User wants to know the recent architectural decisions made in the project.\n- [10:49:34] User wants recent architectural decisions.\n- [12:20:50] Provide recent project history and timeline.\n- [14:01:46] Understand the recent project history and timeline.\n### Rules\n- [09:43:54] When asked about architectural decisions, provide the most recent decisions made in the project.\n- [09:47:26] When explaining architectural decisions, include the motivation or justification for each choice.\n- [10:11:31] When providing project history, include the timeline of recent events and phases.\n- [10:25:43] When answering about project history, include the timeline of recent events and phases.\n### Preferences\n- [09:43:54] Present the architectural decisions as a concise bullet\u2011point list with brief descriptions.\n- [09:58:14] Structure the answer with three clearly labeled sections: Architecture Overview, Recent Decisions, and Current Focus, using bullet points for clarity.\n- [10:23:20] Use bullet points for clarity and brevity in presenting architectural analysis.\n- [10:41:47] Present project history using bullet points for clarity and brevity.\n\nPrevious conversation:\n\n[2026-07-04T16:18:23.026665]\nQUESTION: How does the file observer talks to the memory layer?\nANSWER: {\n  \"answer\": \"The file observer does not communicate directly with the memory layer. It observes events and ingests them as Tier\u202f1 notes into the memory pipeline. The memory pipeline then processes and stores the structured knowledge in the Cognee memory layer via cognee.remember().\",\n  \"reasoning_path\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"component\",\n      \"name\": \"observer\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"component\",\n      \"name\": \"memorypipeline\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"component\",\n      \"name\": \"cognee memory layer\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n[2026-07-04T16:47:39.956561]\nQUESTION: Provide a high-level summary of the architecture\nANSWER: {\n  \"answer\": \"The system is a local-first background memory service that continuously builds and maintains a project's knowledge graph. Its high-level data flow is: Developer actions \u2192 Observer Service (passively detects events, never interprets) \u2192 Event Intelligence (filters out noise such as build folders, caches) \u2192 Memory Pipeline (normalizes events, deduplicates, optionally extracts reasoning via an LLM Provider, then stores structured knowledge via cognee.remember()) \u2192 Cognee Memory Layer (the source of truth, storing knowledge graph, vector embeddings, and metadata in embedded SQLite, LanceDB, and KuzuDB) \u2192 Memory Orchestrator (constructs retrieval requests, calls cognee.recall(), returns normalized output) \u2192 Dashboard (human-facing visualizations) and MCP Server (AI\u2011assistant interface). Key architectural rules enforce a strict separation of concerns: the Observer never interprets, Event Intelligence never stores, the Memory Pipeline never answers questions, Cognee owns all memory, the Orchestrator only orchestrates retrieval, the Dashboard only visualizes, and the MCP Server only exposes memory to external AI tools. Additional guidelines include a unified dataset per project, manual decision notes that bypass the Observer, scheduled improvement cycles, and deterministic graph visualizations that avoid heavyweight exports.\",\n  \"reasoning_path\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"document\",\n      \"name\": \"This chunk is about: - Projects: engraph (Cognee) system - Products: Cognee - Companies: Nvidia - Roles: Developer, Architecture Owner - Concepts: Local-first, Source of Truth, Reasoning Extraction - Components: Observer Service, Event Intelligence, Memory Pipeline, LLM Provider, Cognee Memory, Memory Orchestrator, Dashboard, MCP Server - Events: Git commits, file modifications\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"document\",\n      \"name\": \"ARCHITECTURE.md\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n[2026-07-04T17:02:13.200960]\nQUESTION: What are the recent architectural decisions?\nANSWER: [{\"decision\":\"Built a standalone FastAPI sidecar (Decoupled NIM Gateway) to intercept, sanitize, and translate OpenAI-formatted payloads into strict NVIDIA NIM schemas in real-time.\",\"reason\":\"Prevents event-loop deadlocks and ensures lightning-fast graph ingestion without relying on fragile CLI proxies.\",\"source\":\"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: README.md Status:... [graph, ai, project]\",\"confidence\":\"Confirmed\"},{\"decision\":\"Built the foundational MCP (Model Context Protocol) server for universal AI compatibility.\",\"reason\":\"To allow any compatible AI tool to instantly read the project\u2019s mind.\",\"source\":\"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: README.md Status:... [graph, ai, project]\",\"confidence\":\"Confirmed\"},{\"decision\":\"Created Multi-Hop Detective UI component that traverses the knowledge graph to answer complex architectural questions with live reasoning trace paths.\",\"reason\":\"To provide zero-load reasoning trace visualization, answering complex graph questions without added backend load or latency.\",\"source\":\"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: README.md Status:... [graph, ai, project]\",\"confidence\":\"Confirmed\"},{\"decision\":\"Implemented deterministic graph visualization API (/api/graph/summary) that returns a pruned, fast subgraph in <0.1s.\",\"reason\":\"To avoid crashing the browser with massive unstructured graph pull and achieve rapid rendering.\",\"source\":\"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: README.md Status:... [graph, ai, project]\",\"confidence\":\"Confirmed\"},{\"decision\":\"Implemented self-healing indexing via a robust startup verification protocol against Cognee.\",\"reason\":\"To ensure the Knowledge Graph is perfectly synced and prevent rate-limit flooding on reboot.\",\"source\":\"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: README.md Status:... [graph, ai, project]\",\"confidence\":\"Confirmed\"},{\"decision\":\"Implemented ticking debt detection to monitor 'ghost decisions' (code written without recorded intent).\",\"reason\":\"To nudge developers before knowledge is lost.\",\"source\":\"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: README.md Status:... [graph, ai, project]\",\"confidence\":\"Confirmed\"},{\"decision\":\"Designed the system to be local-first, using LanceDB + KuzuDB for embeddings and graph traversal, backed by Nvidia AI API for reasoning extraction.\",\"reason\":\"To run embeddings and graph traversal entirely local, ensuring fast and private operation.\",\"source\":\"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: README.md Status:... [graph, ai, project]\",\"confidence\":\"Confirmed\"},{\"decision\":\"Enforced the Unified Dataset Rule: every project uses exactly ONE unified dataset to ensure a connected knowledge graph.\",\"reason\":\"To prevent the Knowledge Graph from fracturing across multiple Cognee namespaces.\",\"source\":\"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: CODEBASE_MEMORY.md Status:... [memory, \u2502, phase]\",\"confidence\":\"Confirmed\"},{\"decision\":\"Established a two-tier capture system: Tier 1 automatic observation, Tier 2 manual decision notes only.\",\"reason\":\"To separate automatic observation from manual decision capture.\",\"source\":\"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: CODEBASE_MEMORY.md Status:... [memory, \u2502, phase]\",\"confidence\":\"Confirmed\"},{\"decision\":\"Designed the Observer to be passive; it never interprets events.\",\"reason\":\"To keep observation pure and avoid inference.\",\"source\":\"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: CODEBASE_MEMORY.md Status:... [memory, \u2502, phase]\",\"confidence\":\"Confirmed\"}]\n\n[2026-07-04T17:11:17.172738]\nQUESTION: What are the recent architectural decisions?\nANSWER: [\n  {\n    \"decision\": \"Manual notes are normalized directly as MANUAL_NOTE events, bypassing the file observer.\",\n    \"reason\": \"to ensure accurate decision capture\",\n    \"source\": \"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: CODEBASE_MEMORY.md Status:... [memory, \u2502, phase]\",\n    \"confidence\": \"Confirmed\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"decision\": \"Nudge suppression checks globally across all paths for recent manual decisions.\",\n    \"reason\": \"offering a better developer experience (i.e. \\\"I already explained my reasoning today\\\")\",\n    \"source\": \"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: CODEBASE_MEMORY.md Status:... [memory, \u2502, phase]\",\n    \"confidence\": \"Confirmed\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"decision\": \"Memory Pipeline stages: Normalizer \u2192 Deduplicator \u2192 two paths (reasoning to extract \u2192 LLM Interpretation \u2192 cognee.remember() node_set=decisions; structural change only \u2192 cognee.remember() directly).\",\n    \"reason\": \"to separate reasoning extraction from structural changes and prevent redundant remember() calls\",\n    \"source\": \"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: CODEBASE_MEMORY.md Status:... [memory, \u2502, phase]\",\n    \"confidence\": \"Confirmed\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"decision\": \"Deduplicator prevents redundant remember() calls using content hashing + SQLite log.\",\n    \"reason\": \"to prevent stale state accumulation in the graph\",\n    \"source\": \"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: CODEBASE_MEMORY.md Status:... [memory, \u2502, phase]\",\n    \"confidence\": \"Confirmed\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"decision\": \"Initial indexing runs on first project registration: backfills last 50 commits and existing docs/deps.\",\n    \"reason\": \"to quickly build the knowledge graph from existing project history\",\n    \"source\": \"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: CODEBASE_MEMORY.md Status:... [memory, \u2502, phase]\",\n    \"confidence\": \"Confirmed\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"decision\": \"Unified Dataset Rule: Every project uses exactly ONE unified dataset to ensure a connected knowledge graph.\",\n    \"reason\": \"to prevent the Knowledge Graph from fracturing across multiple Cognee namespaces\",\n    \"source\": \"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: CODEBASE_MEMORY.md Status:... [memory, \u2502, phase]\",\n    \"confidence\": \"Confirmed\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"decision\": \"Every remember() call's data_id UUID must be stored in SQLite log immediately.\",\n    \"reason\": \"required for forget() capability\",\n    \"source\": \"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: CODEBASE_MEMORY.md Status:... [memory, \u2502, phase]\",\n    \"confidence\": \"Confirmed\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"decision\": \"improve() runs globally on the unified dataset, triggered explicitly only: once after initial indexing + every 60 min. Never automatic.\",\n    \"reason\": \"heavy operation (minutes, not milliseconds); always run as async background task\",\n    \"source\": \"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: CODEBASE_MEMORY.md Status:... [memory, \u2502, phase]\",\n    \"confidence\": \"Confirmed\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"decision\": \"Dashboard is read-only; it never edits memory.\",\n    \"reason\": \"it only visualizes memory\",\n    \"source\": \"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: CODEBASE_MEMORY.md Status:... [memory, \u2502, phase]\",\n    \"confidence\": \"Confirmed\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"decision\": \"Memory Orchestrator owns query construction and output formatting; Cognee owns retrieval and ranking.\",\n    \"reason\": \"to maintain separation of concerns; orchestrator does not re-rank results\",\n    \"source\": \"[FILE_MODIFIED - STRUCTURAL] Project File: CODEBASE_MEMORY.md Status:... [memory, \u2502, phase]\",\n    \"confidence\": \"Confirmed\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"decis